      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i'm trying to run this macro for our monthly reconciliation but i keep getting a \"run-time error '1004': application-defined or object-defined error\" on this line:\n\nCells(i, 4).Value = wsRecon.Range(\"B\" & i).Value\n\ncan u tell me why this is happening? here is the sub:\n\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim wsRecon As Worksheet\n    Dim i As Integer\n    Set wsRecon = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Data_Final\")\n    \n    For i = 2 To 500\n        Cells(i, 4).Value = wsRecon.Range(\"B\" & i).Value\n    Next i\nEnd Sub",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The error \"Run-time error '1004'\" usually means that the cell you are trying to read or write is empty, protected, or the range doesn't exist. In your code, you are trying to copy data from column B to column D, but if the source cell in `wsRecon` is blank, Excel throws this error.\n\nTo fix this, you should add a check to ensure the source cell isn't empty before trying to copy it. You can use `If Not IsEmpty(...)` to skip empty rows.\n\nHere is the corrected sub with a safety check added:\n\n```vba\nSub MonthlyRecon()\n    Dim wsRecon As Worksheet\n    Dim i As Integer\n    Set wsRecon = ThisWorkbook.Sheets(\"Recon_Data_Final\")\n    \n    For i = 2 To 500\n        ' Check if the source cell is not empty before copying\n        If Not IsEmpty(wsRecon.Range(\"B\" & i)) Then\n            Cells(i, 4).Value = wsRecon.Range(\"B\" & i).Value\n        End If\n    Next i\nEnd Sub\n```\n\n**Why this works:**\nThe `",
